From a1db919ed12b22c5fa2393f75b0cf9beab8b028f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:51:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: core: start each request in multi-block mode

mmc_blk sets MQRQ_XFER_SINGLE_BLOCK in a request's mmc_queue_req when
that request fails and is requeued, so that the retry goes one sector at
a time. The flag is never cleared. mmc_queue_req lives in the blk-mq
request's private data and is reused for every later request with the
same tag, so after one error every request on that tag is transferred
one sector per command until the queue goes away.

On a microSD card at SDR104 one CRC error left reads at about 5 MB/s:
a trace showed 5700 CMD17 against 45 CMD18 for an 8 MiB read, with a
single data error among them.

Clear the flags with the retry count when a request is first issued.
A requeued request keeps RQF_DONTPREP and so keeps its single-block
retry.

Not yet run on hardware.

Fixes: c7c6d4f51038 ("mmc: block: use single block write in retry")
---
 drivers/mmc/core/queue.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c b/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
index 39fcb66..9da77ed 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
@@ -295,6 +295,7 @@ static blk_status_t mmc_mq_queue_rq(struct blk_mq_hw_ctx *hctx,
 
 	if (!(req->rq_flags & RQF_DONTPREP)) {
 		req_to_mmc_queue_req(req)->retries = 0;
+		req_to_mmc_queue_req(req)->flags = 0;
 		req->rq_flags |= RQF_DONTPREP;
 	}
 
